WEBVTT

NOTE NASA's own caption file for "Exploring Star and Planet Formation" (Captions.vtt on science.nasa.gov), speech cues only, every time moved 3.5 s earlier to match the trimmed starbirth.webm.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:08.469
Newborn stars are found within
brilliant, colorful nebulae.

00:00:11.508 --> 00:00:17.223
However, star formation begins
in dark, dense clouds.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:27.346
Within one vast dark cloud, gravity collapses
thousands of individual dense clumps.

00:00:30.147 --> 00:00:36.877
The core of a massive dense clump will
compress and heat until it forms a protostar.

00:00:39.908 --> 00:00:44.923
A protostar grows as a disk of
gas and dust accretes onto it,

00:00:44.923 --> 00:00:50.907
and some of the accreting material
is ejected along twin opposing jets.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:01:00.953
While the star finishes its formation, planets
build up within the surrounding disk.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:11.138
A few hundred million years later, the
new solar system has assembled.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:22.500
Stars and planets form together, at
billions of sites across our galaxy.
